    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s roster today, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (85.34) and **Cal Raleigh** (79.31) headline our starts as the only players breaching the 75-point threshold. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is the standout play, benefiting from a massive 19% boost due to his matchup against Jacob Lopez; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, his elite profile at the #2 hole makes him our must-start anchor. **Cal Raleigh** similarly thrives in the power department, drawing a favorable 5.92 xERA matchup against Jose Quintana. The combination of park factors and the +19% SP skill adjustment cements these two as our primary engines for RBI and HR production today. \n\nStrategic gains are also found in our outfield and middle infield, where **Jeremiah Jackson** (63.08) and **Daulton Varsho** (70.55) provide significant upside. **Jeremiah Jackson** is a key target for our SB-weighted strategy, as the +2% boost from a slow SP delivery helps him leverage his speed against Gasser. On the bench, **Kyle Karros** (51.75) was the most difficult exclusion; his potential to exploit the favorable park factors was undercut by the inherent risk of a lineup that remains pending and a neutral platoon split against Bryce Miller. We are keeping a close watch on **Will Smith** and **Lawrence Butler**, who both show strong efficiency scores (74.95 and 73.25, respectively) but carry slight risk due to the reliance on projected lineup spots. Ensure all daily cap counts are monitored, particularly for **Alex Freeland**, whose score is lower than preferred; he remains active only to fill the MI slot as we wait for more stability from our bench depth, including **Justin Crawford** and **Masyn Winn**.",
